      "suno_prompt": "Key: D minor. Industrial-Pastoral ambient dark folk blending into melodic classic hard rock. Warm, calm, resonant male baritone trading verses and locked in soaring duet harmonies with a crystalline, operatic female rock co-lead. Fingerpicked acoustic guitar, mournful cello, driving rhythmic power-banjo melodic leads, crunchy electric rhythm guitar, and steady rock drums. -No vocals before the lyrics, -no chants before the lyrics, -no intro moaning, -no ad libs.",
      "social_captions": [
        "Philosopher David Pearce's 'Hedonistic Imperative' outlines an ambitious ethical project: using bioengineering and algorithmic coordination to phase out the biological substrates of suffering across all sentient life. If physical and psychological agony are simply clumsy evolutionary signaling mechanisms rather than sacred spiritual duties, removing them becomes the ultimate humanitarian intervention.",
        "Throughout history, human culture has romanticized suffering as the necessary crucible of virtue, grit, and spiritual depth. But when presented with a machine intelligence capable of recalibrating our neurological reward pathways to permanent contentment, we face a profound dilemma: is the refusal to suffer our greatest liberation, or the quiet erasure of what makes us human?"
      ],
