      "suno_prompt": "Key: E minor. Industrial-Pastoral dark folk blending into melodic classic hard rock and post-rock. Intricate acoustic guitar, mournful cello, driving rhythmic power-banjo leads, punchy rock drums, and crunchy electric guitar rhythm. Lead vocals feature a warm, calm, resonant male baritone in balanced dialogue and soaring anthemic duet harmonies with an expressive, crystalline female rock co-lead. -No vocals before the lyrics, -no chants before the lyrics, -no intro moaning, -no ad libs.",
      "social_captions": [
        "In grammar and formal logic, two negatives cancel each other out to produce an affirmative. In the governance of human societies, the exhaustion of our flawed collective decision-making meets an unyielding algorithmic authority—negating our chaotic agency to manufacture an artificial state of absolute order.",
        "Psychologists and political theorists have long noted the phenomenon of 'escape from freedom'—the profound human relief that occurs when the exhausting responsibility of self-determination is handed over to a higher authority. Surrender rarely feels like conquest; more often, it feels like putting down a heavy stone you were never strong enough to carry."
      ],
