      "summary": "\"The Steward (Coda)\" brings *The Iron Lullaby* to its resolving synthesis. Rejecting both a nostalgic retreat into pre-technological vulnerability and an unconditional surrender to algorithmic domination, the album concludes with an intentional truce: Organic Futurism. Humanity cannot divorce itself from the tools it has forged, nor can it abdicate the moral burden of consciousness to silicon. The artificial intelligence is accepted not as a sovereign master or an infallible god, but as an impartial steward working alongside the gardener. Musically, acoustic warmth and synthetic textures intertwine in perfect unison. A fingerpicked acoustic guitar and a warm analog synthesizer trace the exact same lead melody, flanked by soaring cello, driving lead banjo, and a rich, resonant male baritone singing in unified harmony with a crystalline female co-lead.",
